      "difficulty": "HARD",
      "explanation": "B is correct. If P doubles in 4 years: P(1+R)⁴ = 2P → (1+R)⁴ = 2. For 4P: (1+R)ⁿ = 4 = 2² = [(1+R)⁴]² → (1+R)^8 = 4 → n = 8 years. Rule: if a sum n-tuples in t years, it becomes n²-tuples in 2t years. Since it doubles in 4 years (n=2, t=4), it becomes 4 times in 8 years. Trap: 12 = 4×3 (wrong — not linear at CI); 16 = 4×4 (wrong reasoning).",
      "staleness_risk": 0,
      "answer_source": "generated"
